        "ru-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                "word": "поочерёдно",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "ru",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                        "entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "совершая, происходя по очереди, один за другим"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbb2f030-5fe4-4ac6-aebd-a86bc174216b",
                                "sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                                "text": "Кто только мог, поднялся на ноги, и все поочерёдно стали подходить к царю, получать от него сушёные сливы, которыми он наделял братию из собственных рук."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0ec6ec4-471a-4c0f-92bb-94e3a4520b07",
                                "sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                                "text": "офицеры собирались друг у друга поочерёдно, по вечерам играли в карты."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d435ae7-590e-4581-aa9c-94121fb400fe",
                                "sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                                "text": "С полминуты он постоял за спиной у веселящегося Эдуарда, покачиваясь с пятки на носок и разглядывая всех поочерёдно, словно в первый раз увидел."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "8fd519f0-35b2-4352-a8c5-26c89f9cdbe4",
                        "source_entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "alternately",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alternately",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "df2e8e84-b59e-3253-96cd-53db667bf15a",
                                        "entry_id": "bd988ddd-af6b-31b3-93cf-774746694f64",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In reciprocal succession; succeeding by turns; in alternate order."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "60ba0ab5-f5d8-4716-b2b2-6acaeb9b926b",
                                                "sense_id": "df2e8e84-b59e-3253-96cd-53db667bf15a",
                                                "text": "All night Katerina and I watched alternately, though, I shame to say, I slept more than I watched; and, having first ascertained that there was no change, I came directly hither."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fc7d224-f8d8-4ad1-91ae-88fa973bddce",
                                                "sense_id": "df2e8e84-b59e-3253-96cd-53db667bf15a",
                                                "text": "Tired with the heat and my walk, I threw myself down on the grass in the shadow of the house, where I lay half-asleep enjoying a quiet rest, when I was startled by an unpleasant clamour, the jarring voice of a woman, who was trying by alternately scolding and using pet names to pacify a litter of grunting pigs on the farm."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2980d7a1-8f09-48a4-92e2-ebecaf883bc4",
                                                "sense_id": "df2e8e84-b59e-3253-96cd-53db667bf15a",
                                                "text": "Well, I can't help noticing that you insult me and then you're polite to me alternately."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72665851-2e0a-42eb-a4b8-a39a3457518f",
                                                "sense_id": "df2e8e84-b59e-3253-96cd-53db667bf15a",
                                                "text": "The 2025 timetable would feature two trains per hour, alternately routed via Kirkcaldy (with 11 intermediate stops) and Dunfermline (14 stops), with journey times ranging between 65 and 81 minutes."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "08483303-905f-35b7-ba6a-6f65a8e3978b",
                                        "entry_id": "bd988ddd-af6b-31b3-93cf-774746694f64",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "By alternation; when, in a proportion, the antecedent term is compared with antecedent, and consequent."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4dbad339-06ba-3637-8b5c-679f73ec0afe",
                                        "entry_id": "bd988ddd-af6b-31b3-93cf-774746694f64",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Alternatively."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Canada",
                                            "US",
                                            "not-comparable",
                                            "proscribed",
                                            "sometimes"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5fe98cab-4ab7-4c73-9e31-bfc4fac19197",
                                                "sense_id": "4dbad339-06ba-3637-8b5c-679f73ec0afe",
                                                "text": "Downstairs, he was informed. That is, down the escalators, where there is both a women’s room (often with a line) and a men’s room (almost never with a line). Or alternately, he could ask the station master to buzz him into the “family” bathroom. He opted to go downstairs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a62d62b2-8db3-4a48-9aef-40aa48945558",
                                                "sense_id": "4dbad339-06ba-3637-8b5c-679f73ec0afe",
                                                "text": "Westerners have never quite understood the reverence in Japan for fugu, alternately known in English as puffer fish, globefish or blowfish, of the family Tetraodontidae."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "841eed83-711e-46bb-9c94-39f28778ba59",
                        "source_entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "alternatively",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alternatively",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8061cbf8-6127-392b-9ea2-eeceac26fecb",
                                        "entry_id": "06f0f69d-84d7-3128-b105-9556f088df00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in an alternative way"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "779ab1ee-8865-4fe8-a411-7ddae9a9ff19",
                                                "sense_id": "8061cbf8-6127-392b-9ea2-eeceac26fecb",
                                                "text": "Observers should keep in mind that these efforts at living alternatively are not easily undertaken; indeed, if they were, more people would be doing what they do."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8d2f58bd-3492-452e-b56d-7f00a941e2d7",
                                                "sense_id": "8061cbf8-6127-392b-9ea2-eeceac26fecb",
                                                "text": "Thus, we are creating a new class struggle between those who live within the social system and those who are marginalized or wish to live alternatively."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bee63f05-eded-4453-b668-55f2bee8f115",
                                                "sense_id": "8061cbf8-6127-392b-9ea2-eeceac26fecb",
                                                "text": "Devising obviously asks for what we understand as general creativity, like the ability to take an initiative, to invent, to think alternatively, to associate interestingly, to create metaphors and images."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e130f848-69f0-4f63-bc87-73d2c3ec46b0",
                                                "sense_id": "8061cbf8-6127-392b-9ea2-eeceac26fecb",
                                                "text": "Most people living alternatively have strong pro-environmental values and, unlike many 'greens' in mainstream society, are generally able to apply their values in day-to-day life."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "319499aa-0bb8-3d91-8056-b7dae651576e",
                                        "entry_id": "06f0f69d-84d7-3128-b105-9556f088df00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to link a pair of opposing possibilities."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "conjunctive",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "654fcf3c-9eb3-4c9a-bbb3-c6480e2e6c96",
                        "source_entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "l'un après l'autre",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6c10e9f5-57c9-4950-8e43-a4b183ff72d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "à tour de rôle",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "à tour de rôle",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01deda9a-c145-3938-b03d-dd165d8619ea",
                                        "entry_id": "f028cfbe-84bd-3452-89f2-2acae1ef10f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chacun à son tour ; pas tous à la fois."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "300721a3-47a9-4f42-9b5b-95b0abc0aa2b",
                                                "sense_id": "01deda9a-c145-3938-b03d-dd165d8619ea",
                                                "text": "Les insurgés vont s’asseoir à tour de rôle sur le fauteuil royal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "32045422-6175-4179-a233-5afe76b34c9a",
                                                "sense_id": "01deda9a-c145-3938-b03d-dd165d8619ea",
                                                "text": "En parlant à tour de rôle devant le microphone, nous aurions dû dire que notre victoire était celle de la technique aéronautique française et de la météorologie, beaucoup plus que le triomphe de deux hommes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26eda586-862a-4d23-b32b-9212b8317b37",
                                                "sense_id": "01deda9a-c145-3938-b03d-dd165d8619ea",
                                                "text": "[…] ; les deux danseurs à tour de rôle s’agitaient en frappant sur un tambourin de peaux de phoque. Ce n’était pas beaucoup plus étrange que le charleston ou le black-bottom ; […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "03a1d270-46ee-4a85-94ef-2d40af4bacdd",
                                                "sense_id": "01deda9a-c145-3938-b03d-dd165d8619ea",
                                                "text": "La principale différence entre le Baccara en banque et le Chemin de fer réside en ce que chaque joueur, dans ce dernier jeu, devient banquier à tour de rôle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bab8fe4b-6962-4568-881b-f0f7ca57c60a",
                                                "sense_id": "01deda9a-c145-3938-b03d-dd165d8619ea",
                                                "text": "L’hypokhâgne, c'était du sérieux, du costaud. On ne rigolait pas, en hypokhâgne. On n'était pas là pour enfiler des perles. C'est du moins ce que nous ont répété, à tour de rôle, le proviseur, le censeur, et le surveillant général en chef que tout le monde appelait Bitus mais qui devait se nommer autrement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0379e3d4-3c49-46fb-98e5-7cea27144984",
                                                "sense_id": "01deda9a-c145-3938-b03d-dd165d8619ea",
                                                "text": "Il s'exprimait sans la moindre gêne, en nous regardant à tour de rôle. Le tour de Lena semblait juste revenir un peu plus souvent que le mien."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "325efc41-2174-3554-afac-361d748b5d41",
                                        "entry_id": "f028cfbe-84bd-3452-89f2-2acae1ef10f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Au fur et à mesure."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Plus rare"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "92824b7e-7bbc-4da0-b929-c8c4af9c0824",
                                                "sense_id": "325efc41-2174-3554-afac-361d748b5d41",
                                                "text": "[…], Chlother employait son temps à se promener d’un domaine à l’autre. Il allait de Braine à Attigny, d’Attigny à Compiègne, de Compiègne à Verberie, consommant à tour de rôle, dans ses fermes royales, les provisions en nature qui s’y trouvaient rassemblées, […]."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a34bbbfa-c2ca-3db1-b6ea-0e7ad7885f1c",
                                        "entry_id": "f028cfbe-84bd-3452-89f2-2acae1ef10f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chacun selon son rang."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d43c4952-1ed2-4f49-aea0-887b2ae464b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "successivement",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "successivement",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "198bef3c-af56-3ad0-96c8-536d59c9b1e2",
                                        "entry_id": "1ced2862-b287-36d0-bb58-cbcfbed06dd0",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "L’un après l’autre."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27976698-f311-4297-8c85-0188cc6c2139",
                                                "sense_id": "198bef3c-af56-3ad0-96c8-536d59c9b1e2",
                                                "text": "Après une présentation rapide de l’aérogare nᵒ 1 de Roissy-en-France, avec son corps central et ses sept satellites, l’auteur décrit successivement les divers équipements réalisés dans cet ensemble."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8c088ede-ebda-4589-9c0a-aea1c1868dd0",
                                                "sense_id": "198bef3c-af56-3ad0-96c8-536d59c9b1e2",
                                                "text": "Tous ont successivement combattu pour ou contre les Jacobins, selon les temps & les circonstances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "31e1c9cc-7c07-4677-b6f4-2443e50fb6f7",
                                                "sense_id": "198bef3c-af56-3ad0-96c8-536d59c9b1e2",
                                                "text": "Azemmour est une ville très ancienne. D’origine berbère ou carthaginoise, elle passa successivement sous la domination romaine, vandale, byzantine et arabe. En 1518, les Portugais s’en emparèrent, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d5f34891-b226-428c-9bd2-49f855a32db3",
                                                "sense_id": "198bef3c-af56-3ad0-96c8-536d59c9b1e2",
                                                "text": "Bert effleura successivement un bon nombre de métiers : il fut groom dans un magasin de nouveautés et chez un médecin, garçon de pharmacie, apprenti plombier, griffonneur d’adresses, garçon laitier, « golf caddie », et enfin aide-mécanicien chez un loueur et réparateur de bicyclettes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e6ec93e0-4345-48d7-b75f-0dd3ee3d184d",
                                                "sense_id": "198bef3c-af56-3ad0-96c8-536d59c9b1e2",
                                                "text": "Seront examinés successivement : l’efficacité graminicide, l’efficacité dicotylédonicide et la sélectivité à l’égard du colza de l’association propyzamide + diuron (Kerb ultra)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "650c64cb-dd21-4c1c-96cb-db32e084a21b",
                                                "sense_id": "198bef3c-af56-3ad0-96c8-536d59c9b1e2",
                                                "text": "Des planètes dont les différentes parties ne jouissent que successivement d’une lumière empruntée,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "925800ac-d588-4b64-bb60-18f47fe9239f",
                        "source_entry_id": "14a72c8d-f250-3e22-9b61-135a14f2a5bd",
                        "source_sense_id": "91c68425-9b2a-33d6-83df-82c0cb1e32c2",
                        "target_lang_word": "alternativement",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alternativement",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "73eb64f8-b34e-3e2b-ba2d-a085d9d250e1",
                                        "entry_id": "1764a69a-c228-3059-a39c-01bf1954d633",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tour à tour ; l’un après l’autre ; à tour de rôle."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "28d5faf1-530d-4974-b1c4-1e585ecb04e8",
                                                "sense_id": "73eb64f8-b34e-3e2b-ba2d-a085d9d250e1",
                                                "text": "Et tous les trois, ayant pris la tête de Iaokanann, s’en allèrent du côté de la Galilée.\nComme elle était très lourde, ils la portaient alternativement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2b326505-398f-4518-adae-fb9206959eba",
                                                "sense_id": "73eb64f8-b34e-3e2b-ba2d-a085d9d250e1",
                                                "text": "Helmy buvait ses paroles, contemplait ses yeux alternativement enflammés et tendres, et caressait lentement la main qu'elle lui abandonnait."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
